  "scientific_verdict": "Suppression/Erosion Mechanism Confirmed. HRRB successfully reduces false bridge events (118 -> 108, -10 events; 9 images cured), but it pays for this reduction with a severe increase in true-crack breakage (35 -> 75, +114%) and a substantial drop in recall (-6.55%). Residual magnitude analysis confirms that detail_residual acts almost entirely as a negative suppression field (93.4% of images have 0 positive residual pixels). It does not function as an independent discriminative feature stream, but rather performs prediction-space erosion/suppression."
